.TH tkutldrag n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutldrag
.PP
Let the user reorder \fBtablelist\fR rows with the mouse and get a callback after each move. Wraps tablelist's \fB\-movablerows\fR. Library\-neutral.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutldrag 0.1
.CE
.PP
Requires \fBTk\fR and \fBtablelist\fR.
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutldrag::enable  tbl ?options?   ;# -> select mode now in use
::tkutils::tkutldrag::disable tbl
::tkutils::tkutldrag::order   tbl ?parent?    ;# -> ids of the children of parent
.CE
.PP
\fBorder\fR returns the row ids (\fB\-name\fR) of the children of \fBparent\fR (default \fBroot\fR) in display order; rows without a name give their key. Store it to keep a user\-defined order.
.SS Options
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-command\fR	\fB{}\fR	called after a move as \fBcmd tbl id parent position\fR
\fB\-samelevel\fR	\fB1\fR	only reorder among siblings, never a new parent
\fB\-acceptchild\fR	\fB{}\fR	own \fB\-acceptchildcommand\fR (overrides \fB\-samelevel\fR)
\fB\-acceptdrop\fR	\fB{}\fR	own \fB\-acceptdropcommand\fR (overrides \fB\-samelevel\fR)
.TE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require Tk
package require tablelist_tile
package require tkutils::tkutldrag

proc moved {tbl id parent pos} {
    saveOrder [::tkutils::tkutldrag::order $tbl]
}
::tkutils::tkutldrag::enable .t -command moved
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
\fB\-movablerows\fR works only with select mode \fBsingle\fR or \fBmultiple\fR. \fBenable\fR changes \fBbrowse\fR to \fBsingle\fR and \fBextended\fR to \fBmultiple\fR.
.IP \(bu
With \fB\-samelevel 1\fR a row in a tree can be dropped only before a sibling; the end of a child list other than the top level is not a drop target.
.IP \(bu
Escape cancels a drag (tablelist).
.IP \(bu
A table sorted by column shows its sort order; after the user drags a row, call \fB$tbl resetsortinfo\fR if the arrow should go.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLDRAG OPTION}\fR.
